+Editor's Note (this revision)
+
+   This copy of RFC 3007 has been amended to define an externally-signed
+   update policy (new Section 4.5), under which a zone's SIG (RRSIG)
+   records are generated by the update principal and verified by the
+   server, rather than generated by the server from an online zone key.
+   This removes the requirement, described in the original Section 5,
+   that zone key material be held on a network-connected host.  Because
+   the server then cannot sign, the policy also changes how updates are
+   applied (Section 4.5.5: complete replacement, a client-supplied SOA
+   serial) and adds control data and a version prerequisite (Section
+   4.5.6).  Page pagination has not been reflowed.  See [SAZU] for the
+   full mechanism this amendment enables.
+
